# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variable template.
#
# Copy to `.env` for local development:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env*` is git-ignored except for this file. NEVER put a real secret here.
#
# Every variable below is declared in the schema at src/lib/env/schema.ts and
# is validated at startup. Adding a variable here without adding it there means
# nothing reads it; adding it there without a default means the application
# refuses to start until it is set.
#
# Payment, invoicing, email and object-storage credentials are deliberately
# ABSENT. No provider has been chosen (TBD.md B1, B2, I1, I2) and no code reads
# them, so listing placeholder keys would only describe integrations that do
# not exist.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# PostgreSQL connection string. REQUIRED - there is no default, because a
# fallback would silently point a misconfigured deployment at the wrong
# database.
#
# The value below matches docker-compose.yml, so `npm run db:up` plus this file
# is a working local setup. These are development-only credentials.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://jewelry:jewelry_local_dev@localhost:5433/jewelry?schema=public"

# Canonical public origin: canonical URLs, sitemap, robots, Open Graph images.
# Optional - defaults to http://localhost:3000. The production domain is TBD.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- media
#
# Media storage is S3-compatible: Cloudflare R2 in production, MinIO locally
# (docs/MEDIA_STORAGE_DECISION.md).
#
# ALL SIX ARE OPTIONAL. With none of them set the application boots, the
# catalog renders, and images fall back to the placeholder surface. Set either
# all six or none - a partial configuration is a deployment mistake and is
# rejected loudly rather than treated as "unconfigured".
#
# The values below match the MinIO service in docker-compose.yml. To use them:
#   npm run media:up && npm run media:init
#
# MEDIA_S3_ENDPOINT="http://localhost:9000"
# MEDIA_S3_REGION="us-east-1"
# MEDIA_S3_BUCKET="jewelry-media"
# MEDIA_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID="jewelry_dev"
# MEDIA_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="jewelry_local_dev"
# MEDIA_PUBLIC_BASE_URL="http://localhost:9000/jewelry-media"
